WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.602
Welcome to Module 7, Advanced Python Techniques.

00:00:03.602 --> 00:00:08.014
Up to this point, we have spent a lot of time building a strong

00:00:08.014 --> 00:00:09.635
foundation in Python.

00:00:09.635 --> 00:00:14.047
We have worked with variables, conditions, loops, functions,

00:00:14.047 --> 00:00:17.469
data structures, and ways to organize our code.

00:00:17.469 --> 00:00:21.701
In this module, we are going to take some of those ideas and

00:00:21.701 --> 00:00:26.113
look at more compact and more powerful ways to write Python.

00:00:26.113 --> 00:00:31.426
You will see techniques such as list comprehensions, lambda functions,

00:00:31.426 --> 00:00:35.928
and generators. We will also spend some time on debugging and

00:00:35.928 --> 00:00:40.880
code efficiency. I want to emphasize something from the beginning.

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:45.743
Advanced Python does not necessarily mean writing the shortest

00:00:45.743 --> 00:00:51.145
code possible. Short code can sometimes become difficult to understand.

00:00:51.145 --> 00:00:55.738
Our goal is to write code that is clear, useful, and appropriate

00:00:55.738 --> 00:00:57.989
for the problem we are solving.

00:00:57.989 --> 00:01:02.761
These techniques are especially helpful in analytics because

00:01:02.761 --> 00:01:07.173
we often need to filter values, transform data, sort records,

00:01:07.173 --> 00:01:09.425
or process large collections.

00:01:09.425 --> 00:01:14.107
As we move through the examples, try to focus less on memorizing

00:01:14.107 --> 00:01:19.239
the syntax and more on understanding what each technique is helping

00:01:19.239 --> 00:01:20.320
us accomplish.
